„­bible_version£KJV¤book*§chapter¨sectionsš…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ$Jesus went unto the mount of Olives.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ{And early in the morning he came again into the temple, and all the people came unto him; and he sat down, and taught them.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqAnd the scribes and Pharisees brought unto him a woman taken in adultery; and when they had set her in the midst,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙMthey say unto him, Master, this woman was taken in adultery, in the very act.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTNow Moses in the law commanded us, that such should be stoned: but what sayest thou?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸThis they said, tempting him, that they might have to accuse him. But Jesus stooped down, and with his finger wrote on the ground, as though he heard them not.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‘So when they continued asking him, he lifted up himself, and said unto them, He that is without sin among you, let him first cast a stone at her.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3And again he stooped down, and wrote on the ground.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÂAnd they which heard it, being convicted by their own conscience, went out one by one, beginning at the eldest, even unto the last: and Jesus was left alone, and the woman standing in the midst.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ’When Jesus had lifted up himself, and saw none but the woman, he said unto her, Woman, where are those thine accusers? hath no man condemned thee?¦layout ªlast_verse
„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`She said, No man, Lord. And Jesus said unto her, Neither do I condemn thee: go, and sin no more.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Then spake Jesus again unto them, saying, I am the light of the world: he that followeth me shall not walk in darkness, but shall have the light of life.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^The Pharisees therefore said unto him, Thou bearest record of thyself; thy record is not true.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¹Jesus answered and said unto them, Though I bear record of myself, yet my record is true: for I know whence I came, and whither I go; but ye cannot tell whence I come, and whither I go.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ)Ye judge after the flesh; I judge no man.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ_And yet if I judge, my judgment is true: for I am not alone, but I and the Father that sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙFIt is also written in your law, that the testimony of two men is true.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙXI am one that bear witness of myself, and the Father that sent me beareth witness of me.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ™Then said they unto him, Where is thy Father? Jesus answered, Ye neither know me, nor my Father: if ye had known me, ye should have known my Father also.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThese words spake Jesus in the treasury, as he taught in the temple: and no man laid hands on him; for his hour was not yet come.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦versesš„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ}Then said Jesus again unto them, I go my way, and ye shall seek me, and shall die in your sins: whither I go, ye cannot come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYThen said the Jews, Will he kill himself? because he saith, Whither I go, ye cannot come.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙjAnd he said unto them, Ye are from beneath; I am from above: ye are of this world; I am not of this world.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙyI said therefore unto you, that ye shall die in your sins: for if ye believe not that I am he, ye shall die in your sins.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙxThen said they unto him, Who art thou? And Jesus saith unto them, Even the same that I said unto you from the beginning.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŒI have many things to say and to judge of you: but he that sent me is true; and I speak to the world those things which I have heard of him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ8They understood not that he spake to them of the Father.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙºThen said Jesus unto them, When ye have lifted up the Son of man, then shall ye know that I am he, and that I do nothing of myself; but as my Father hath taught me, I speak these things.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpAnd he that sent me is with me: the Father hath not left me alone; for I do always those things that please him.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ.As he spake these words, many believed on him.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book*§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse$¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpThen said Jesus to those Jews which believed on him, If ye continue in my word, then are ye my disciples indeed;¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ?and ye shall know the truth, and the truth shall make you free.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvThey answered him, We be Abraham's seed, and were never in bondage to any man: how sayest thou, Ye shall be made free?¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙdJesus answered them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Whosoever committeth sin is the servant of sin.¦layout ªlast_verse"„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLAnd the servant abideth not in the house for ever: but the Son abideth ever.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBIf the Son therefore shall make you free, ye shall be free indeed.¦layout ªlast_verse$…¤book*§chapter«first_verse%ªlast_verse)¦verses•„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`I know that ye are Abraham's seed; but ye seek to kill me, because my word hath no place in you.¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbI speak that which I have seen with my Father: and ye do that which ye have seen with your father.¦layout ªlast_verse&„¥verse'¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThey answered and said unto him, Abraham is our father. Jesus saith unto them, If ye were Abraham's children, ye would do the works of Abraham.¦layout ªlast_verse'„¥verse(¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpBut now ye seek to kill me, a man that hath told you the truth, which I have heard of God: this did not Abraham.¦layout ªlast_verse(„¥verse)¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙsYe do the deeds of your father. Then said they to him, We be not born of fornication; we have one Father, even God.¦layout ªlast_verse)…¤book*§chapter«first_verse*ªlast_verse/¦verses–„¥verse*¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“Jesus said unto them, If God were your Father, ye would love me: for I proceeded forth and came from God; neither came I of myself, but he sent me.¦layout ªlast_verse*„¥verse+¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHWhy do ye not understand my speech? even because ye cannot hear my word.¦layout ªlast_verse+„¥verse,¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÚYe are of your father the devil, and the lusts of your father ye will do. He was a murderer from the beginning, and abode not in the truth, because there is no truth in him. When he speaketh a lie, he speaketh of his own: for he is a liar, and the father of it.¦layout ªlast_verse,„¥verse-¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ4And because I tell you the truth, ye believe me not.¦layout ªlast_verse-„¥verse.¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙTWhich of you convinceth me of sin? And if I say the truth, why do ye not believe me?¦layout ªlast_verse.„¥verse/¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]He that is of God heareth God's words: ye therefore hear them not, because ye are not of God.¦layout ªlast_verse/…¤book*§chapter«first_verse0ªlast_verse3¦verses”„¥verse0¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙgThen answered the Jews, and said unto him, Say we not well that thou art a Samaritan, and hast a devil?¦layout ªlast_verse0„¥verse1¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙSJesus answered, I have not a devil; but I honour my Father, and ye do dishonour me.¦layout ªlast_verse1„¥verse2¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd I seek not mine own glory: there is one that seeketh and judgeth.¦layout ªlast_verse2„¥verse3¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙRVerily, verily, I say unto you, If a man keep my saying, he shall never see death.¦layout ªlast_verse3…¤book*§chapter«first_verse4ªlast_verse8¦verses•„¥verse4¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¬Then said the Jews unto him, Now we know that thou hast a devil. Abraham is dead, and the prophets; and thou sayest, If a man keep my saying, he shall never taste of death.¦layout ªlast_verse4„¥verse5¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙmArt thou greater than our father Abraham, which is dead? and the prophets are dead: whom makest thou thyself?¦layout ªlast_verse5„¥verse6¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙJesus answered, If I honour myself, my honour is nothing: it is my Father that honoureth me; of whom ye say, that he is your God:¦layout ªlast_verse6„¥verse7¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ•yet ye have not known him; but I know him: and if I should say, I know him not, I shall be a liar like unto you: but I know him, and keep his saying.¦layout ªlast_verse7„¥verse8¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙHYour father Abraham rejoiced to see my day: and he saw it, and was glad.¦layout ªlast_verse8…¤book*§chapter«first_verse9ªlast_verse;¦verses“„¥verse9¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙZThen said the Jews unto him, Thou art not yet fifty years old, and hast thou seen Abraham?¦layout ªlast_verse9„¥verse:¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOJesus said unto them, Verily, verily, I say unto you, Before Abraham was, I am.¦layout ªlast_verse:„¥verse;¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙThen took they up stones to cast at him: but Jesus hid himself, and went out of the temple, going through the midst of them, and so passed by.¦layout ªlast_verse;